    <decisions>
        <description>Checks whether the Accepted Quote already has a Contract. If it does, that Contract is reused.</description>
        <name>Contract_Exists</name>
        <label>Contract Exists?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Create_Contract</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No Contract</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Has_Contract</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Accepted_Quote.ContractId</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Assign_Existing_Contract</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Has Contract</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>Checks whether an Order already exists for the Accepted Quote. If it does, it is activated instead of creating another one.</description>
        <name>Order_Exists</name>
        <label>Order Exists?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Create_Orders</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No Order</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Has_Order</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Existing_Order.Id</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Activate_Orders</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Has Order</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>Stops when no Accepted Quote was found.</description>
        <name>Quote_Found</name>
        <label>Quote Found?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Set_No_Quote_Error</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No Quote</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Found</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Accepted_Quote.Id</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Contract_Exists</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Found</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>Only continues when the Opportunity exists and Closed Won Automation Complete is unchecked, so a direct call can&apos;t create duplicates.</description>
        <name>Ready_To_Run</name>
        <label>Ready to Run?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Skip</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Run</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Opportunity.Id</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsNull</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>Get_Opportunity.Closed_Won_Automation_Complete__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Get_Accepted_Quote</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Run</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Called by Opportunity - Closed Won - After Save with the Opportunity Id. Finds the Opportunity&apos;s Accepted Quote and stops if there isn&apos;t one. Creates the Contract with the native Create Contract action (net unit prices saved as contract prices) and activates it. Creates the Order with the native Create Orders From Quote action and activates it, which fires Order - Create Assets. Then checks Closed Won Automation Complete, clears Closed Won Automation Error and links the Contract to the Opportunity. Re-uses a Contract or Order that already exists for the Quote, and does nothing if the automation has already completed, so re-running it doesn&apos;t create duplicates. Any error is written to Closed Won Automation Error and sent through the Fault Path Subflow. The renewal Opportunity and Quote are created later by Order - Assets Created - Create Renewal, once the Assets exist.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>Closed Won Revenue Automation {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Closed Won Revenue Automation</label>
